Gradient descent \eqref{GD} can be framed as the update of the state of a discrete-time linear time-invariant system
\begin{equation} 
	{x_{k + 1}} = {x_k} + {u_k}, \label{ztfc} 
\end{equation} where $x_k\in\mathbb{R}^{np}$ and $u_k=-\lambda \nabla F(x_k)\in\mathbb{R}^{np}$ are the state and control, respectively. 
Inspired by this, we aim to propose a numerical method to solve the problem \eqref{P2} by finding a new control law ${u_k}$ to update the state $x_k$ within the framework of the optimal control problem, i.e.,
  \begin{equation}
  	\begin{array}{l}
  		\mathop {{\rm{min}}}\limits_u {\rm{ }}\sum\limits_{k = 0}^N {(F({x_k}) + \frac{1}{2}u_k^{\rm{T}}} Ru_k^{}) + F({x_{N + 1}}),\\
  		{\rm subject\ to}{\rm {\; \eqref{ztfc}}},
  	\end{array}\label{OCP}
  \end{equation}
  where the initial condition ${x_0}$ is given, $N$ is the time horizon. The terminal cost is $F({x_{N+1}})$ and $R\in\mathbb{S}^{np}_{++}$ is the control weighted matrix.

